title    Fixed Changes
tempo    92
beats    4
steps    4

voice pad   epiano vol=0.5 center=E4
voice kick  kick
voice snare snare
voice hat   hat vol=0.4
# Bass: acoustic upright, slightly short gate so the syncopated 16ths articulate
# instead of smearing, and enough level to sit under the epiano pad (voiced near E4).
voice bass  upright vol=0.95 gate=0.85

pattern A
pad   | [Am7]--------------- | [D7]--------------- | [Gmaj7]--------------- | [Cmaj7]--------------- |
kick  | x... ..x. x... .... | % | % | % |
snare | .... x... .... x... | % | % | % |
hat   | x.x. x.x. x.x. x.x. | % | % | % |
# Bass intent (ii-V-I-IV in G):
# - Every downbeat states the root low (A1, D2, G1, C2) and lands with the kick on step 1;
#   the kick's syncopated hits on the "a" of beat 2 and on beat 3 also get bass notes,
#   so bass and kick act as one rhythmic unit, with ghosted notes filling the gap.
# - The second half of each bar is a 16th-note run that outlines the chord (3rds, 7ths)
#   and ends one half step from the next root, so each bar line is a chromatic resolution:
#   Eb2->D2 (from above), Ab2->G (tritone-sub colour on D7, resolving by half step in pitch class, then dropping to the deep G1), B1->C2 (leading tone),
#   Bb1->A1 (from above, closing the loop).
# - Colour tones: G2 (b7) leaps over Am7, a passing Eb3 (b9) on D7 hinting D7b9,
#   F#2 and B2 (major 7ths) placed on kick hits in the Gmaj7 and Cmaj7 bars.
bass  | A1---! . A1?? G2- E2- C3 B2- A2 G2 Eb2 | D2-- . D2?? . A1- F#2- A2 C3 Eb3? D3 C3 Ab2 | G1---! . D2?? F#2- G2- B2 D3- B2 G2 B1 | C2--- . G2?? B2- E2- G2 E2 D2 C2 B1 Bb1 |

loop A
